Spec: discovery

Purpose:
  Serve the discovery document of the diagnostic API's aggregated group: answer
    @discovery_handler with the fixed @APIResourceList JSON for @API_GROUP/@API_VERSION so
    the front-proxy sees the `admin.vynil.solidite.fr/v1` group, hand out the two group
    constants, and define the `group`/`version`/`resources` and `name`/`namespaced`/`kind`
    wire shapes.

Owns:
  ./discovery.rs

References:
  ./server.rs — mounts @discovery_handler as the sole handler of the group base path
    `/apis/admin.vynil.solidite.fr/v1` inside @create_router and defines its own duplicate
    constants; the mount path is this endpoint's observable contract but lives there, not
    in this file.
  /box/vynil/systems/diag_service.yaml.hbs — the aggregated @APIService
    `v1.admin.vynil.solidite.fr` (group `admin.vynil.solidite.fr`, version `v1`) that makes
    requests for the group base path reach this handler through the kube apiserver.

Must:
  @discovery_handler is unconditional and input-free: the whole file imports only
    @axum::Json and @serde, it reads no extractors, state, headers, arguments, environment
    or Kubernetes object, and the response is identical on every call and independent of
    who calls — the instance route authenticates first, the discovery route has no such
    step.
  The @axum::Json body always serializes to exactly the fixed document
    `{"group":"admin.vynil.solidite.fr","version":"v1","resources":[]}`:
    `group` and `version` interpolate @API_GROUP and @API_VERSION via @to_string and are
    the file's only value sources beyond the literal empty `vec![]`, and serde applies its
    default no-rename field naming.
  Serving that @axum::Json through the @create_router mount yields `200` with content type
    `application/json`; @discovery_handler is a parameterless `pub async fn` with the bare
    @axum::Json return type, so it never reaches @crate::DiagError, a status code it does
    not itself define, or a @panic!.
  @APIResourceList and @APIResource are `pub` with every field private and no constructor
    or accessor: outside this module the types exist only through their derived
    @Serialize/@Deserialize (that is how input arrives) plus @std::fmt::Debug and @Clone.
  The wire shape comes from the derives with no serde attribute anywhere: an @APIResource
    is the keys `name` (@String), `namespaced` (@bool) and `kind` (@String), and an
    @APIResourceList is the keys `group` (@String), `version` (@String) and `resources`
    (@Vec<@APIResource>).
  `resources` is only ever the empty list in reachable execution: @discovery_handler always
    builds the literal empty `vec![]`, @APIResource is constructed nowhere in the
    workspace, and no cache, refresh interval, retry, timeout or expiration exists here.

Depends on:
  axum `0.8.9` locked in `/Cargo.lock` (`0.8` in `/server/Cargo.toml`) — @axum::Json is the
    only runtime collaborator, supplying the response envelope and its content type.
  serde `1.0.228` locked in `/Cargo.lock` with feature `derive` (`/server/Cargo.toml`) —
    the derives define every field's JSON name and the deserialization half of the public
    surface; nothing reads the JSON by hand.

Exposes:
  @API_GROUP — @pub const @API_GROUP: &@str = `admin.vynil.solidite.fr`, the aggregated
    group the server is registered under.
  @API_VERSION — @pub const @API_VERSION: &@str = `v1`, the group version advertised.
  @APIResource — `pub struct` deriving @Serialize, @Deserialize, @std::fmt::Debug and
    @Clone; private fields `name`: @String, `namespaced`: @bool, `kind`: @String.
  @APIResourceList — `pub struct` deriving @Serialize, @Deserialize, @std::fmt::Debug and
    @Clone; private fields `group`: @String, `version`: @String, `resources`:
    @Vec<@APIResource>.
  @discovery_handler — `pub async fn @discovery_handler() -> @axum::Json<@APIResourceList>`;
    an infallible static document, mounted GET-only by `./server.rs`.

Accepts:
  Nothing on the request side: @discovery_handler matches `GET` on the group base path with
    no extractor, so no body, query, path parameter, header, credential or @crate::AppState
    value changes the response.
  Any JSON document keyed `group`, `version` and `resources`, each resource keyed `name`,
    `namespaced` and `kind`, deserializes into @APIResourceList/@APIResource; the derives
    validate nothing further and no code in this file validates a shape.

Returns:
  The fixed document of Must, always.

Raises:
  No runtime failure channel: the return type is a bare @axum::Json, so @discovery_handler
    cannot yield @crate::DiagError or any other error value, and its body — two string
    interpolations and an empty `vec![]` — has no failure or panic path.

Tasks:
  [ ] Cover the exact document: @discovery_handler() awaited directly, or a router `GET` of
      the group base path, returns `200` with the JSON body pinned key for key.
  [ ] Cover deserialization of a populated list — with one or more name/namespaced/kind
      entries — to pin the wire shape that no producer in the workspace can emit today;
      include the derived @std::fmt::Debug and @Clone behaviour.
  [ ] Cover that the discovery route answers independently of authentication on the
      instance router, freezing today's behaviour before any authz decision is taken.
  [?] @APIResource and the `resources` list of @APIResourceList are never populated, and
      @APIResource is never constructed in the workspace (private fields block external
      construction), so the endpoint advertises zero resources even though the parent spec
      names this module "Package and instance discovery". Unfilled — decide later: list the
      diagnostics resources or trim the types.
  [?] A populated @APIResourceList could only come from deserialization — no constructor or
      accessor exists — yet no code deserializes it and it is never sent anywhere either.
      Decide later: keep the round-trip derives or shrink @Serialize/@Deserialize/@Clone/
      @std::fmt::Debug.
  [?] `./server.rs` declares duplicates of @API_GROUP/@API_VERSION as `pub` constants,
      never reads either copy, and hardcodes the same two strings in the route literals —
      three sources of one value. Decide later which copy becomes canonical.
  [?] Discovery answers unauthenticated while the parent spec asks every read to be
      authorized, and the file's own doc comment says "Handle the discovery endpoint"
      although nothing is discovered dynamically. Decide later: gate the route, document
      the exemption, or fill the handler.
  [?] `namespaced` is typed for real discovery, but the served instance paths under
      `/apis/admin.vynil.solidite.fr/v1/namespaces/` are not `@kube` resources registered
      in this group, so a future populated list needs a namespaced-vs-cluster mapping that
      exists nowhere yet. Decide later what it would hold.

Done when:
  Every Scenario below maps to a green test, each `[?]` above is a decision or a removal,
    and `cargo test -p server` is green.

Scenario: Group base path returns the fixed discovery document
  Given the @create_router app or a bare @discovery_handler call
  When a `GET` reaches the group base path
  Then the response is `200` with content type `application/json` and the exact body
    `{"group":"admin.vynil.solidite.fr","version":"v1","resources":[]}`
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Response is independent of the caller and of the cluster
  Given three requests carrying no identity, an unauthenticated identity and an
    authenticated identity, with no reachable API server
  When @discovery_handler answers each
  Then all three bodies are identical with `resources` empty
  And no Kubernetes object is read
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Populated list deserializes although nothing serializes one
  Given a JSON document with `group` `g`, `version` `v` and one resource entry `name` `n`,
    `namespaced` `true`, `kind` `K`
  When it deserializes into @APIResourceList
  Then the single @APIResource carries those three values
  But this file never builds such a list — @discovery_handler keeps `resources` empty
  No mapped test exists.

Example:
  Served body: `{"group":"admin.vynil.solidite.fr","version":"v1","resources":[]}`
  Derived @std::fmt::Debug form: `APIResourceList { group: "g", version: "v", resources: [APIResource { name: "n", namespaced: true, kind: "K" }] }`
